                                                              "take":  "This is a legitimate regime-change signal, not just a contrarian hot take. When the 10-year spread between stocks and bonds gets this stretched, mean reversion has historically followedÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âeither through bond rallies, equity corrections, or both. Investors who are 100% equities are not just taking duration risk; they are implicitly betting this historical relationship stays broken indefinitely. Adding intermediate Treasuries or investment-grade credit here is not a defensive moveÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã¢â‚¬Âit is a high-conviction trade with an unusually clear valuation rationale.",
